# TEST FIXTURE - NOT ORGANIZATIONAL TRUTH, AND NOT A RUN THAT HAPPENED.
#
# One complete trace summary, invented to exercise the L3 vocabulary and the L3 shapes.
# It is shaped exactly like what semantic_layer.trace.project writes for a real run:
# the run and its spans as PROV activities, the pack it used and the rollups it left
# behind as PROV entities, and both spellings of every edge - the trace vocabulary's
# and PROV-O's - because no reasoner is ever run here and a consumer that speaks only
# PROV has to be able to read this without being told about trc:.
#
# Fixtures are minted under .../fixture/l3/, which no recorded run ever uses, so a
# fixture can never be mistaken for evidence about something that actually ran. The
# pack, observation and agent it names are the fixture ones committed elsewhere: naming
# them is what a trace is for, and asserting anything about them is what it may never
# do.

@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix trc:  <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/trace#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

@prefix run:     <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/fixture/l3/run/> .
@prefix span:    <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/fixture/l3/span/4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736/> .
@prefix outcome: <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/fixture/l3/outcome/> .
@prefix metric:  <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/fixture/l3/metric/4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736/> .
@prefix finding: <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/fixture/l3/finding/4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736/> .
@prefix pack:    <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/fixture/l3/pack/> .

